IO-13: report invalid cross-section geometry as ERROR 119 naming the link

When xsect_setParams() refuses a link's geometry (Geom1 <= 0, sediment depth
not below the diameter, an unknown size code, a missing width, ...),
link_readXsectParams() reported ERROR 211 "invalid number" with an empty
token, which does not say which value or which rule is at fault. Report
ERR_XSECT ("invalid cross section for Link <name>") instead.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-13_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/link.c b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
index 31925e1..cad7fcf 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/link.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/link.c
@@ -247,7 +247,7 @@ int link_readXsectParams(char* tok[], int ntoks)
         }
         if ( !xsect_setParams(&Link[j].xsect, k, x, UCF(LENGTH)) )
         {
-            return error_setInpError(ERR_NUMBER, "");
+            return error_setInpError(ERR_XSECT, tok[0]);
         }
 
         // --- parse number of barrels if present
